   "user": "O_oNevermore",
   "message": "the algorithmic information theory of emergence posits that levels of emergence (physics vs chemistry vs biology etc) are determined almost entirely by the input string that is being compressed (which is determined by an observer class probably, but from the perspective of a universal observer how the input string is constructed can be abstracted away imo)\n\nthe levels are drops on the compression function\n\nin my mind the level of emergence determines the sign systems too. it determines which sign systems can survive at that level of description\n\nso frames are determined by the level of emergence we are at and therefore the compression function and therefore are objective too\n\nframes/languages are just as objective as facts\n\nthe fact that there are various failure modes (infinitely many) doesn't mean things become relative\n\nthat's my current understanding",
   "timestamp": "2026-09-11T07:09:28.688000+00:00",
